---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description={`How ${site.name} handles analytics, ads, and email. Nothing here asks a child for personal information.`} path="/privacy/">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>This site is free. You can download a PDF without an account. These are coloring pages for a parent or a teacher to print.</p>
    <h2>What you do here</h2>
    <p>Reading a page and downloading a PDF does not ask for a name, an email, or a payment. If you email {site.email}, I get whatever you write, and I use it to write back.</p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>Google Analytics counts visits, so I can see which sets get printed and which pages get opened. Cloudflare may count visits too. I use those counts to see how the site is used. I don't sell a profile of you.</p>
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>The pages have spaces for Google ads. Google ads may show when the ad account is connected. The coloring pages stay free. You can control the ads you see at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">Google's ad settings</a>.</p>
    <h2>Pinterest</h2>
    <p>A lot of people arrive from Pinterest. If the Pinterest tag is on, Pinterest may measure visits that came from a pin. The pin pictures are the coloring sets, so you can save a pile of pages.</p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>I wrote this for adults who print pages for children. It is not a service directed at children under 13. There are no child accounts, no chat, and no place for a child to send personal information. Please don't put a child's name or photo in an email unless you need to. A description of the page is enough.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this page: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
